! mcp_bootstrap_p135.strap -- "THE CONCEPTOR", printed page 135.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.142, header READ AND NOT ASSUMED:
! the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041   PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID EE000001   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 135".
!
! >>> A NEW PUNCHED DECK STARTS HERE. <<<  The card-serial column
! restarts at EE000001 on line 1; printed p.128 was still punching
! EB0003xx.  The serials run EE000001..EE000055 over FIFTY-SIX
! lines, because EE000032 IS PUNCHED TWICE -- lines 32 and 33
! ("P ERR EX  SIC, S COM IC" and "B , S COMM") both carry it.
! Verified at 800 dpi, both digits clean.  SO THE SERIAL COLUMN IS
! NOT A LINE COUNT ON THIS DECK; do not use it to check for a
! dropped row.
!
! WHAT THE PAGE IS.  The Conceptor: the MCP's console-interrupt
! handler.  Lines 4-7 are its own English description -- "P CON E1
! IS THE ENTRY PT FROM RECEPTOR IF CS INTERRUPT ON ALONE." and
! "P CON E2 IS THE ENTRY PT IF CS INTERRUPT IS NOT ON ALONE AND
! THE SETUP BIT IS ON."  It selects the MCP unit in the CST, turns
! the channel-op / set-up / read bits on, plants a read into the
! UAT and issues it (WRESL1), then on the way back out turns the
! same three bits off and decodes the typed message's end code.
!
! TAIL SCOPE.  printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." moved the
! origin to 0o215000 and pp.99+ are OUTSIDE the "TAIL,(2)G" block
! that printed p.2 opened and printed p.98 line 37 closed.  Names
! here may legitimately repeat names from pp.2-98 at different
! addresses.  Nothing on this page collides with anything I could
! find; recorded for the record, not fixed.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOIN, BOTH ENDS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> BACKWARD: THE PAGE PRINTS "SLC,$" AND THAT IS A FREE
! WITNESS. <<<  Line 8 is "216620.40 *   SLC,$".  An SLC emits
! nothing, so its printed LOCATION *is* the location counter
! arriving from printed p.134 -- an independent reading of the
! join, printed by IBM's own assembler.  THE DECK WRITES A HARD
! "SLC, (8)216620.40" so it assembles standalone, and that hard
! origin ASSERTS the value rather than checking it (a hard SLC
! cannot disagree with the arriving counter; it overrides it).
! pp.129-134 are not transcribed by me and I did not verify the
! backward join -- when p.134 lands, compare its last location
! against 216620.40 BY HAND.  That comparison is the only thing
! that closes this end.
!
! >>> FORWARD: CLOSED, AND IT CHECKS OUT. <<<  Line 56 is a half
! word at 216660.40, so the counter reaches 216661.00, and printed
! p.136 (PDF p.143) line 1 PRINTS 216661.00 ("SIC, G KONEC").
! Read off the page, not assumed.
!
! >>> THE ADDRESS CHAIN CLOSES END TO END INSIDE THE PAGE. <<<
! Over the FORTY-FIVE storage rows, 216620.40 .. 216660.40: every
! row's printed address plus its own length equals the next row's
! printed address, with no gap and no overlap, across all of them.
! Line 8 also prints a location but is not part of the chain --
! the SLC spends nothing, so its 216620.40 is the SAME address
! line 9 prints, not the one before it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LINES THAT COMPILE NOTHING
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! TEN comment cards: lines 1-7, 45, 49 and 51.  Lines 1-3 are the
! asterisk box around the heading, 4-7 the English above, and 45,
! 49, 51 are continuations of the comment on the row above them
! ("-PRET-WHOSE MESSAGE WAS IT", "-ON ALONE", "-*PP*").  Each
! carries the "-" in the one-character column and has LOCATION and
! BINARY OUTPUT both empty.
! Line 8 PRINTS a location (216620.40) but emits nothing: it is
! the SLC.  So 56 lines = 10 comment cards + 1 SLC + 45 rows that
! produce bits, and there are 45 !CHECK lines below.
!
! LISTING MARKS.  Every line number carries the ordinary asterisk
! after it ("9*", "56*"); that is the column, not a mark.  THREE
! lines carry a SECOND asterisk after the LOCATION -- lines 8
! (216620.40), 23 (216633.00) and 42 (216647.00) -- the
! unexplained marker of docs/listing_typography.md item 12.  It is
! NOT "the SLC row gets it": line 23 is an RD and line 42 a BBZ,
! and printed p.109 line 5's SLC,$ carries none.  No mark changes
! a compiled bit.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS SETTLED, AND HOW
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> "G ODBOC" (line 48), AND IT IS AN O IN POSITION 1 AND AN O
! IN POSITION 4. <<<  The name is round-D-B-round-round and this
! drum opens round glyphs, so shape alone cannot do it.  MEASURED,
! as mean ink in the middle band of the right quarter of each
! glyph, at 1600 dpi, on BOTH printings:
!
!   printed p.135 line 48 (the reference)   O=.12 D=.31 B=.62 O=.55 C=.00
!   printed p.137 line  9 (the definition)  O=.07 D=.31 B=.63 O=.08 C=.00
!
! Position 4 measures .55 on p.135 -- a closed bowl, so it is an
! O, and on p.137 the SAME character measures .08, which fixes
! .07-.12 as "damaged O" on this drum.  Position 5 measures
! EXACTLY .00 on both pages, which no O does.  So positions 1 and
! 4 are O and position 5 is C.
! THE SECOND, INDEPENDENT READING IS THE WORDLIST.  This
! programmer's G-prefixed labels are CZECH: G KONEC (konec, end),
! G ZPET (zpet, back), G VRAT (vrat, return) and G MISTO (misto,
! place) -- all four READ off printed p.136, not OCR'd.  (A fifth,
! at 217047 on printed p.138, OCRs as "G CKOLC" and is probably
! OKOLO, around; I did NOT render it, so it is not evidence.)
! ODBOC is "odboc", branch off, which is exactly what line 48's
! BZAE does.  "CDBCC" is not a word in anything.
!
! "P DBRET" (line 54) is settled by its DEFINING CARD, printed
! p.137 line 12, "216736.40  000012.03 01  PDBRET  LVI,$1,PCDEF2"
! -- the D has the straight vertical left stem -- and by its own
! comment here, "-IF YES GO TO *DB*".
!
! EVERY ROUND GLYPH IN AN OCTAL FIELD on this page is a 0; the
! page prints "COCCOO.70" for "000000.70" constantly.  That is not
! a per-row ink gauge and no hex byte below was settled on it.
! The bytes were settled on WHAT PRODUCED THEM: every one of the
! forty-five rows is reproduced bit-for-bit by the assembler from
! the statement, except line 53 (see below), so each byte is
! confirmed by the statement that made it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE HALF WORD IS OBSERVED; THE BIT INSIDE IT IS NOT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Externals SYN'd off a printed branch or LVI are pinned only to
! the HALF WORD -- bit offsets 0-31 all encode identically, so the
! ".0" written below is a CONVENTION, not a reading.  Bit 32 DOES
! show, and this page exercises it in both directions, which is
! why the ".40"s are real:
!   PDBRET  216736.40  line 54 prints 216736.76 -- leading 1 in
!           the offset is the half-word select, and p.137 line 12
!           PRINTS the defining card at 216736.40.  Confirmed from
!           both ends.
!   PERREX  216640.40  DEFINED on this page (line 32); line 43's
!           "PERREX-1.0" prints 216637.74, again with the select
!           bit set.
!   SCOMIC  215470.40  and SCOMM 215470.00 -- the two halves of
!           one word, and printed p.116's deck already carries
!           !SYM SCOMM 215470.00 and !SYM SCOMIC 215470.40.  This
!           page confirms both independently.
! Where a symbol is back-derived and only ".0" is observable, the
! !CHECK note says so.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHERE THE SYMBOLS COME FROM
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The eight field-offset SYNs are printed p.99's own definitions,
! verbatim from the decks that landed them, and every one is
! confirmed by a row here:
!   SUNIT  (BU,3),0.56  line  9 prints 000000.70   (0.56 -> .70)
!   SSEL   (BU,1),0.39  line 11 prints 000000.47
!   SUNA   (BU,25),0.0  lines 13/14/55/56 print 000000.26/.30
!   SIOINS (BU,64),4.0  line 16 prints 000004.02
!   SCHOP  (BU,1),0.26  lines 17/41 print 000000.32
!   SSETUP (BU,1),0.31  lines 18/39 print 000000.37
!   SRD    (BU,1),0.57  lines 19/40 print 000000.71
!   SRETAD (BU,19),5.0  line 21 prints 000005.37
!
! KSUPP  216242.00  LANDED by printed p.128, which DEFINES it
!                   ("K SUPP NOP,K COMM R").  Lines 24 and 36 here
!                   print 216242.03 and 216242.10.
! STLR   215230.00  LANDED by pp.116/117/118.  THREE OFFSETS ON
!                   ONE PAGE, and all three resolve: "STLR+8.9"
!                   prints 215240.11, "+8.10" prints 215240.12,
!                   "+8.13" prints 215240.15.  The bare decimal
!                   bit offset prints octal, as the rule says.
! SCOMM  215470.00  LANDED by printed p.116 (line 37, "S COMM
! SCOMIC 215470.40  B,MCOMD"; line 38, "S COMIC VF,0").
! MIOREJ 221261.00  NEW here.  Line 25 prints 221261.10 00.  The
!                   volume OCR carries EIGHT more references, all
!                   "221261.1C CO  B,M IO REJ", at 217576.40,
!                   217624.00, 217665.40, 217672.40, 217710.40,
!                   217716.40 and 217745.00 -- every one with bit
!                   18 clear, so the half word is 0.  I did not
!                   find its defining card; the offset within the
!                   half word is unobservable.
! PTEMBF 216743.00  NEW.  Its DEFINING CARD is in the volume OCR,
!                   printed p.137: "216743.00 *  000015.00
!                   P TEM BF  DR(BU,64),(13)" -- a thirteen-word
!                   buffer, which is what lines 26, 50 and 52 use
!                   it as.  Lines 50 and 52 print 216745.77 and
!                   216746.00, i.e. PTEMBF+2.63 and +3.0.
! PEPGK  217024.00  NEW.  Defining card in the volume OCR,
!                   printed p.137: "217024.00  P EPGK  (IQS*)
!                   ...( BU), MESSAGE NOT ACCEPTED EPGK ERROR*".
!                   An entry-mode message constant.  Line 27 here
!                   prints 217024.03.
! PUK    217030.00  NEW.  Same page, next card: "217030.00  PUK
!                   (IQS*)..(BU), MESSAGE NOT ACCEPTED UK ERROR*".
!                   Line 30 prints 217030.03.
! GODBOC 216735.00  NEW.  Defining card printed p.137 line 9,
!                   "216735.00  217042.03 01  G ODBOC  LVI,$1,
!                   P MSG ER".  Line 48 prints 216735.36.
! PPPRET 216722.00  NEW.  Defining card in the volume OCR,
!                   printed p.137: "216722.00  ...  P PP RET
!                   BZB,S UN ASG+1.0($11),G ERROR".  A second
!                   reference at 216702.40 prints "216722.36 C2
!                   BAE,P PP RET".  Line 50 here prints 216722.34.
! PDBRET 216736.40  NEW.  See above -- printed p.137 line 12.
!
! >>> TWO-SIDED AGREEMENT WITH printed p.128. <<<  That deck SYNs
! PCONE2 at (8)216644.0 off its line 22, "B,PCONE2" -> 216644.10.
! THIS page DEFINES PCONE2, and line 39 prints 216644.00.  The two
! pages agree from opposite ends.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! SPELLINGS SUBSTITUTED, AND THE ASSEMBLER GAP BEHIND THEM
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> A SYMBOL PRINTED WITH BLANKS WORKS IN A VFL OPERAND AND NOT
! IN AN ADDRESS FIELD. <<<  strap_asm's blanked-symbol rule lives
! in eval_expr (strap/strap_asm.py, the _BLANKED_SYMBOL block
! around line 656) and eval_addr_field -- the path every branch,
! B, LV, LVI, SIC and SVA address goes down -- DOES NOT HAVE IT.
! MEASURED, each form fed to the assembler on its own (the page
! prints SCHOP, SSETUP and SRD CLOSED UP, so lines 17-19 and
! 39-41 needed no substitution at all):
!
!   CM0000(BU,3), S UNIT($10)    OK   <- eval_expr path, kept as
!   CM0000(BU,1),S SEL($2)       OK      printed in the deck
!   CM1111(BU,1),S CH OP($10),0  OK   (a probe; the page prints
!                                      SCHOP closed up on lines 17
!                                      and 41, so no substitution
!                                      was needed there)
!   LV,$11,S UN A($10)           FAIL  undefined symbol 'S'
!   LVI,$1, P EPGK               FAIL  undefined symbol 'P'
!   B, P ERR EX                  FAIL  undefined symbol 'P'
!   B, K SUPP                    FAIL  undefined symbol 'K'
!   SIC, S COM IC / B , S COMM   FAIL  undefined symbol 'S'
!   BBZ, STLR +8.9, P EPGK E     FAIL  undefined symbol 'P'
!   BZAE,G ODBOC                 FAIL  undefined symbol 'G'
!   BAE,P DBRET                  FAIL  undefined symbol 'P'
!   LV,$11,S UNA($10)            FAIL  undefined symbol 'S'
!
! and a blanked symbol with an OPERATOR beside it fails on BOTH
! paths, because eval_expr's rule requires the whole field to be
! letters, digits and blanks:
!   CM1111(BU,1),S SEL+1.($2)    FAIL  undefined symbol 'S'
!   C0011(BU,8),P TEMBF+3.0      FAIL  undefined symbol 'P'
!   BZB,P TEMBF+2.63,P PPRET     FAIL  undefined symbol 'P'
!
! So the deck writes the closed-up spelling in those places.  Each
! is BIT-IDENTICAL (STRAP ignores blanks inside a name) and every
! printed form is kept verbatim in its !CHECK note below.  THE
! PRINTED FORM WAS TRIED FIRST IN EVERY CASE; the two blanked
! operands the assembler accepts (lines 9 and 11) are written AS
! PRINTED.
!
! A NAME PRINTED WITH BLANKS cannot be written at all -- the deck
! format takes the name from column 1 to the first blank, so
! "P EPGK E  CNOP" is read as the mnemonic "EPGK E  CNOP".  Five
! names on this page are affected: P CON E1, P RENT, P EPGK E,
! P ERR EX, P CON E2.  All written closed up.
!
! >>> P EPGK AND P EPGK E ARE TWO DIFFERENT SYMBOLS, 0o166 WORDS
! APART, AND THE PAGE REFERENCES BOTH. <<<  PEPGK is the message
! constant at 217024.00 (line 27 prints 217024.03) and PEPGKE is
! the label at 216636.00 that line 42 branches to (prints
! 216636.34).  Closing up the blanks keeps them distinct; a parser
! that stopped at the first blank would merge them.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> ONE ROW IS LEFT FAILING, AND IT IS A REAL ASSEMBLER GAP. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LINE 53, "KFI(BU,8),(2)1111 1110", prints 774000.00 80
! 410000.23 10.  The assembler produces 312000.00 80 410000.23 10.
!
! 774000 octal is 11111110 left-justified in the 18-bit immediate
! field, which is the datum the statement names.  strap_asm
! instead TREATS THE BLANK AS A TERM SEPARATOR and evaluates
! "(2)1111" + "1110" = 15 + 1110 decimal = 1125, truncated to the
! 8-bit field as 1125-1024 = 101 = 0b01100101, which is exactly
! the 312000 it prints.  MEASURED across three data values, each
! fed on its own:
!
!   printed form            assembles     listing prints
!   (2)1111 1110            312000.00     774000.00     (= 15+1110)
!   (2)1111 1101            270000.00                   (= 15+1101)
!   (2)1111 1100            266000.00                   (= 15+1100)
!   (2)11111110  (no blank) 774000.00     774000.00     correct
!
! THE CODE THAT KNOWS THE RULE EXISTS AND IS NOT ON THIS PATH.
! strap_asm's parse_dd_literal (near the bottom of the file) is
! headed "BLANKS INSIDE A RADIX LITERAL ARE GROUPING, not
! separators" and strips them correctly -- but it is reached only
! for DD literals, never for VFL immediate data.
!
! I HAVE LEFT THE PRINTED FORM IN THE DECK AND THE ROW FAILING.
! Writing "(2)11111110" would make it pass and would hide a
! SILENT WRONG ANSWER -- the assembler does not reject the printed
! spelling, it miscompiles it -- which is worse than a rejection
! and will recur: the volume OCR shows the same construction at
! printed p.136 line 13 ("(2)1111 1101"), line 15 ("(2)1111
! 1011"), and printed p.138 lines 43 and 48 ("(2)1111 1100" and
! "(2)1111 1110", the latter compiling to the identical
! 774000.00 80 410000.23 10 and so confirming this row's bits
! from a second, independent printing).
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

SUNIT   SYN(BU,3), 0.56              ! p.99 line 39  -UNIT NUMBER
SSEL    SYN(BU,1), 0.39              ! p.99 line 32  -SELECT
SUNA    SYN(BU,25), 0.0              ! p.99 line 20  -UNIT AREA TABLE
SIOINS  SYN(BU,64), 4.0              ! p.101 line 17 -IO INSTR. LAST
SCHOP   SYN(BU,1), 0.26              ! p.99          -CHAN OPERATING
SSETUP  SYN(BU,1), 0.31              ! p.99 line 25  -PSEUDO-OP SET-UP
SRD     SYN(BU,1), 0.57              ! p.99 line 45  -READ
SRETAD  SYN(BU,19), 5.0              ! p.101 line 18 -RETURN ADDRESS

KSUPP   SYN, (8)216242.0             ! p.128 defines it; bit unobservable
STLR    SYN, (8)215230.0             ! p.117 defines it ("S T LR DRZ")
SCOMM   SYN, (8)215470.0             ! p.116 line 37
SCOMIC  SYN, (8)215470.40            ! p.116 line 38 -- the .40 IS checked
MIOREJ  SYN, (8)221261.0             ! line 25; bit within half word unobservable
PTEMBF  SYN, (8)216743.0             ! p.137 "P TEM BF DR(BU,64),(13)"
PEPGK   SYN, (8)217024.0             ! p.137 message constant
PUK     SYN, (8)217030.0             ! p.137 message constant
GODBOC  SYN, (8)216735.0             ! p.137 line 9 defines it
PPPRET  SYN, (8)216722.0             ! p.137 "P PP RET"
PDBRET  SYN, (8)216736.40            ! p.137 line 12 -- the .40 IS checked

        SLC, (8)216620.40            ! line 8 PRINTS "SLC,$" at 216620.40

PCONE1  CM0000(BU,3), S UNIT($10)    ! line  9  -SET UNIT NO EQUAL TO MCP IN CST
        LV,$2,0($10)                 ! line 10  -GET ADDR OF UST
        CM0000(BU,1),S SEL($2)       ! line 11  -SELECT MCP UNIT
        CM1111(BU,1),SSEL+1.($2)     ! line 12  -UNSELECT PP UNIT
PRENT   LV,$11,SUNA($10)             ! line 13  -SELECT MCP UST
        LV,$12,SUNA($11)             ! line 14  -OBTAIN MCP UAT
        SVA,$14,WRESL1               ! line 15
        TI,1,WRESL1,SIOINS($12)      ! line 16  -PLACE RD INSTR IN UAT
        CM1111(BU,1),SCHOP($10),0    ! line 17  -CHAN OP ON
        CM1111(BU,1),SSETUP($11),0   ! line 18  -SET UP ON
        CM1111(BU,1),SRD($11),0      ! line 19  -READ ON
        LVI,$15,PCONE2               ! line 20
        SV,$15,SRETAD($12)           ! line 21
        CNOP                         ! line 22
WRESL1  RD,0,WPCW                    ! line 23
        LVI,$1,KSUPP                 ! line 24
        B,MIOREJ                     ! line 25
WPCW    CW,PTEMBF,13,WPCW            ! line 26
PEPGKE  LVI,$1,PEPGK                 ! line 27
        LVI,$2, 4.0                  ! line 28
        B, PERREX                    ! line 29
        LVI,$1,PUK                   ! line 30
        LVI,$2,4.0                   ! line 31
PERREX  SIC, SCOMIC                  ! line 32
        B , SCOMM                    ! line 33
        ,0($1)                       ! line 34
        ,0($2)                       ! line 35
        B, KSUPP                     ! line 36
        BCSZ,PRENT                   ! line 37
        B,PRENT                      ! line 38  -SAFETY FACTOR
PCONE2  CM0000(BU,1),SSETUP($11)     ! line 39  -SET UP OFF
        CM0000(BU,1),SRD($11)        ! line 40  -RD OFF
        CM0000(BU,1),SCHOP($10)      ! line 41  -CHAN OP OFF
        BBZ, STLR+8.9, PEPGKE        ! line 42  -EPGK INTERRUPT IS ON
        BBZ,STLR+8.10,PERREX-1.0     ! line 43  -IF UK
        BBZ,STLR+8.13,PCONE2-1.0     ! line 44  -IF CS
        L(BU,5),STLR+8.9,50          ! line 46  -LOAD I/O INDICATORS
        KFI(BU,4),(2)0001,51         ! line 47  -COMPARE IF ONLY*EOP*INDIC. IS ON
        BZAE,GODBOC                  ! line 48
        BZB,PTEMBF+2.63,PPPRET       ! line 50
        C0011(BU,8),PTEMBF+3.0       ! line 52  -LEADING 8BITS OF THE 4TH WORD
        KFI(BU,8),(2)1111 1110       ! line 53  -IS IT *END*CODE  <<< FAILS, see header
        BAE,PDBRET                   ! line 54  -IF YES GO TO *DB*
        LV,$11,SUNA($10)             ! line 55  -SELECT*MCP*UNIT ST.TAB.ADDR.
        LV,$12,SUNA($11)             ! line 56  -OBTAIN*MCP*UNIT AREA TAB.ADDR.

